alwaysApply: false
description: Follow this template for PR descriptions. Use when writing or editing a PR description or preparing a PR for review.
---
### Guidelines for generating the PR:
1. **Holistic Analysis:** Analyze the **entire diff** as a single block. Ignore chat history/incremental steps.
2. **Jira Link:** Extract the Jira key from branch/commits. Generate Header: `## [KEY-123](https://your-domain.atlassian.net/browse/KEY-123)`. Omit if no key is found.
3. **Why Section:** Write a **single, punchy bullet point** on purpose/value. **Do not** describe technical implementation.
4. **What Section:** List actual changes from the **full diff**, ordered by impact.
5. **Attention Points:** Use `### !Attention Points!` **only** for risks or **pending** tasks (style/docs/tests). Omit section if everything is complete.
6. **Strict Omission:** **NO "N/A" or Meta-commentary**. Delete lines or sections entirely if they have no data.
7. **Omit Screenshots:** Remove the "Screenshots" section if tests are only CI/CD/Checks or if no tests were run.
8. **Clean Output:** Remove all instructional text and bracketed hints from the final response.

---

